1
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,484
This is data on 142

2
00:00:04,484 --> 00:00:07,523
countries from 1952 to 2007.

3
00:00:07,523 --> 00:00:11,813
In 1952, average life expectancy, weighted

4
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:15,030
by population, was 48.9 years.

5
00:00:15,030 --> 00:00:17,264
By 2007 it was 68.9

6
00:00:17,264 --> 00:00:20,035
years, a change of +20.0.

7
00:00:20,035 --> 00:00:23,163
So where did that change come

8
00:00:23,163 --> 00:00:26,380
from, and who got left behind?

9
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:31,027
Split by continent, every continent's average was

10
00:00:31,027 --> 00:00:33,899
higher in 2007 than in 1952.

11
00:00:33,899 --> 00:00:36,096
Asia had the largest

12
00:00:36,096 --> 00:00:38,461
gain of any continent:

13
00:00:38,461 --> 00:00:41,503
from 42.9 years to 69.4 years.

14
00:00:41,503 --> 00:00:45,981
Meanwhile, Africa's average stayed between 53.3

15
00:00:45,981 --> 00:00:48,769
and 53.4 from 1992 to 2002.

16
00:00:48,769 --> 00:00:51,810
For a decade, it barely moved.

17
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:53,864
Put the first year next

18
00:00:53,864 --> 00:00:55,705
to the last, and the

19
00:00:55,705 --> 00:00:58,114
gaps tell a different story.

20
00:00:58,114 --> 00:01:01,159
The gap between Asia and Oceania went

21
00:01:01,159 --> 00:01:03,709
from 26.3 years to 11.7 years.

22
00:01:03,709 --> 00:01:06,117
But Africa was lowest at the

23
00:01:06,117 --> 00:01:08,808
start, at 38.8, and still lowest

24
00:01:08,808 --> 00:01:10,650
at the end, at 54.6.

25
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:14,943
Country by country, Oman gained the most:

26
00:01:14,943 --> 00:01:16,496
38.1 years.

27
00:01:16,496 --> 00:01:20,697
Vietnam gained 33.8, and Indonesia 33.2.

28
00:01:20,697 --> 00:01:23,712
Not everyone moved forward.

29
00:01:23,712 --> 00:01:28,096
In Zimbabwe, life expectancy was 5.0 years

30
00:01:28,096 --> 00:01:31,110
lower in 2007 than in 1952.

31
00:01:31,110 --> 00:01:33,795
Each bubble is a country, sized

32
00:01:33,795 --> 00:01:36,625
by population, and they all drift

33
00:01:36,625 --> 00:01:38,511
up and to the right.

34
00:01:38,511 --> 00:01:42,067
In 2007, the correlation between log income

35
00:01:42,067 --> 00:01:45,404
per person and life expectancy was 0.81.

36
00:01:45,404 --> 00:01:47,799
In 1952, 5 of 142 countries

37
00:01:47,799 --> 00:01:50,048
were at 70 years or more;

38
00:01:50,048 --> 00:01:51,717
in 2007, 83 were.

39
00:01:51,717 --> 00:01:54,910
That link is strong, but a correlation

40
00:01:54,910 --> 00:01:58,030
alone can't tell us what causes what.

41
00:01:58,030 --> 00:02:00,212
These are averages, so they hide

42
00:02:00,212 --> 00:02:02,625
big differences inside each country.

43
00:02:02,625 --> 00:02:05,554
The data comes from the Gapminder Foundation,

44
00:02:05,554 --> 00:02:08,023
and the dataset link and the analysis

45
00:02:08,023 --> 00:02:09,976
code are in the description.

46
00:02:09,976 --> 00:02:11,067
I'm Compiled.

47
00:02:11,067 --> 00:02:12,790
See you in the next one.
